From 260234656fac47f92d5c61e1dbde0003da37add5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:03:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): stop guidance that invites agent_owned_block
 refusals [daveey]

Coach store, week of 2026-10-27: 62 agent_owned_block refusals in 60 sessions
(kanban_block 55, kanban_create 7). Every refused call followed text Hermes
itself gave the agent:

- worker prompt step 4 / Do-NOT, the stop nudge and turn recovery prescribed
  `kanban_block(reason=...)` with no kind or human_request (kind=None refusals);
- kanban_block `reason` said "for needs_input/capability write numbered steps
  the human must perform", and `kind` said those kinds "surface to a human",
  so asks went into reason (25 capability, 14 needs_input refusals);
- kanban_create `initial_status` never said 'blocked' needs human_request, so
  asks went into body (6 real asks);
- kanban_continue's exhaustion error prescribed
  kanban_block(kind='transient', reason='continuation_exhausted: ...'), which
  the tool/CLI guard refused before block_task's agent-triage routing ran
  (8 refusals; only kb.block_task was tested, never the entry points).

Changes:
- guard skips only the DB-verified exhausted-budget block
  (is_exhausted_budget_block), which block_task routes to agent triage;
  every other ask-less block is still refused;
- refusals (block + create) carry a copyable human_request skeleton; the
  create refusal names parents=/kanban_schedule for agent waits;
- kanban_block/kanban_create schema text and worker prompts name
  human_request and the agent-wait routes.

Tests: tests/tools/test_kanban_agent_owned_block_guidance.py covers tool and
CLI paths for block and create refusal text, schema/prompt guidance, the
exhaustion route (tool + CLI), and that the guard still refuses.
